# perf study 22 §3 — THE COPY-TRAFFIC PROBE.  NOT FOR MERGE.
#
# Applied to src/eval/nnue/sota_accumulator.rs at commit 7237f6d (arms 1+1b+2).
# Adds ONE extra accumulator-pair copy per evaluated node — 5120 B read from the
# parent entry, 5120 B written to a reused heap scratch, `black_box`'d so it
# cannot be eliminated.  That is the memory traffic of exactly one more
# accumulator-pair fold, i.e. what deleting one of the two accumulator stacks
# would give back.  Measured: +80.1 cycles/node (+1.83%), +157.4 instructions
# (+2.591%), +55.38 L1d misses (+8.95%); node-identical, hash-identical.
#
# Reproduce: apply the three hunks below, build with
# docs/research/perf-artifacts-22/scripts/build22.sh, then
# scripts/panel22.sh <base> <probe> 10.

